# Event extraction projection V2 audit checklist

- [ ] VMS-41 v1 code and frozen evidence remain untouched.
- [ ] Candidate JSON rejects unknown fields, booleans-as-integers and non-finite values.
- [ ] Candidate events contain byte offsets only; runner recomputes every span hash.
- [ ] Occurrence history may contain source-backed events beyond hidden coarse anchors.
- [ ] One event cannot absorb two hidden anchors and every required anchor maps exactly once.
- [ ] Required relationships are structured typed paths, not arbitrary reachability.
- [ ] Forbidden relations and forbidden typed paths fail closed.
- [ ] Status-at-occurrence and later-resolution are judged independently.
- [ ] Every MERGE has at least two parents and one contribution object per parent.
- [ ] Required origin anchors map injectively to distinct MERGE parents.
- [ ] Pairwise-incomparable frontier checks exclude the final MERGE edges.
- [ ] Candidate bytes, event/edge counts and path search/enumeration all have stable fail-closed budgets.
- [ ] A mechanical PASS remains pending blind manual semantic audit.
- [ ] No model, Solver, database, network or filesystem mutation occurs in this module.
